  "preliminary_interpretation": {
    "confirmed": [
      "The actual official Test 2 passed with 50 successful purchases, 350 refusals, zero errors and a reported 12.89-second fire() wall clock.",
      "Connection counts increased while sampled sessions were idle or starting and no active checkout call was observed, followed by many active checkout sessions and lock-related waits.",
      "Tuple locks, transaction-ID locks, internal LockManager/BufferContent LWLocks and WalSync I/O waits were observed during active checkout calls.",
      "The run returned to two baseline non-monitor client connections; fixture checks passed before and after.",
      "No separate blocking-chain, CPU utilization, per-wait-duration, barrier-release or disk-latency measurements were collected."
    ],
    "hypotheses": [
      "Connected buyers waiting at the Python barrier plausibly explain much of the idle/ClientRead connection-ramp phase.",
      "Concurrent updates of one fixture product plausibly explain checkout lock contention; exact blocking objects and chains were not captured.",
      "Lock-manager concurrency overhead and row/transaction contention may both contribute after checkout starts; their shares of total wall time cannot be determined from snapshots.",
      "The sampled WalSync waits may affect the serialized commit path, even though only one backend was observed in this event at a time."
    ],
    "not_established": "No single primary bottleneck, exact connection-versus-checkout timing split, or causal explanation for the difference from the prior 16.10-second run has been established."
  },
  "execution_notes": [
    "Only monitoring SQL was changed; no new implementation or benchmark scripts were saved.",
    "The unsupported/ambiguous trailing positional 80 in the old watch invocation was replaced with explicit interval=0.5 count=240. The old run was not reproduced and its termination cause remains unconfirmed.",
    "The diagnostic driver executed the actual monitoring SELECT repeatedly through an autocommit connection until after the official process, fixture recheck and settled samples; it did not run psql watch.",
    "DATABASE_URL was absent from process/user/machine environment. A process-only value was constructed privately from kloudkart_rebuild settings, validated for 127.0.0.1:5433, and inherited by the unchanged race process.",
    "No sampling/SQL/race execution errors were observed. Activity sampling itself slowed to a 1.771-second query and a 2.286-second interval at peak load.",
    "Unchanged row counts and empty fixture checks establish count reconciliation, not a row-by-row historical data comparison. The official test advances generated-ID sequences and creates/deletes its authorized synthetic fixtures."
  ]
